# ---- the campaign's named places (2026-11-18) -------------------------------------------------------------------
# The campaign (ASSETS TO USE/bay_city_3d) names places: a courthouse, two hospitals, two banks, a penitentiary, an
# airport, a power plant, a fire station. Each stands where the script's own coordinates fall on the Bay map
# (plan_campaign.py), also where the drawing labels the place elsewhere: the user, 2026-11-18, "Seguir o roteiro".
# The project's building models have none of these kinds, so each is a building of its own: place_mesh.py builds it
# (structure of the same name) and the place's sector keeps its ground free. clear_lots.py takes away the buildings
# that stood there, without planning the sector's other buildings again.
#   kind    what place_mesh.py builds
#   sector  the sector it stands in
#   centre  middle of its site; front: the direction its front faces, degrees from east, counter-clockwise
#   size    the site, metres across the front by metres deep
#   z       street-surface height of the site's ground (block ground is a kerb above)
#   street  metres from the site's front edge to the middle of the street (or square) in front of it: where the
#           review cameras stand (0: none, the cameras stand on the site itself)
# A site's own coordinates: a across the front (to the left of someone leaving by the front door), b towards the
# front, both from the centre. place_point() and place_ring() turn them into map coordinates.
